    {
      "review_id": "ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNzdE1YQ2tBRRAB",
      "author": "SRINIVASA RAO PURAM",
      "rating": 5,
      "relative_date": "Edited a year ago",
      "text": "Since I couldn’t get an immediate appointment with a reputed skin specialist in Guntur, I consulted Dr. J. Sowjanya. She promptly started treatment and modified the medication twice based on my response. Later, she advised a skin biopsy, which fortunately came back negative.\n\nMeanwhile, I managed to get an appointment with the reputed doctor who had previously treated my skin issues. However, after examining me, he concluded that the disease was incurable. He even returned the consultation fee and didn’t prescribe any treatment. That was a low point for me—I had lost hope.\n\nDespite this, I continued Dr. Sowjanya’s treatment. She again adjusted the medication and suggested it might be a seasonal condition. This time, she changed the antihistamine, and to my surprise, the rashes began to disappear. Eventually, they cleared up completely.\n\nThough she is relatively junior, Dr. Sowjanya’s patient and thoughtful approach—trying different medications with care—led to a successful outcome. I’m truly thankful to her.\n\nThis incident clearly shows that even experienced experts can sometimes misdiagnose, while a sincere and methodical approach can make all the difference.\n\nI strongly recommend Dr. J. Sowjanya. She is calm, non-commercial, and cautious in her treatment. She avoids unnecessary antibiotics and steroids, aiming for real healing rather than temporary symptom suppression.",
